    "Hundvåg Tunnel, stretching 5.5 kilometres, burrows beneath Byfjorden, linking Stavanger’s mainland to the island of Hundvåg as part of the 2019‑opened Ryfast tunnel network.",
    "The tunnel’s western portal meets the Eiganes Tunnel in Stavanger, while its eastern exit lies just shy of the Ryfylke Tunnel entrance, a longer fjord‑crossing route.",
    "Opened in 2019, Hundvåg Tunnel is a key artery in the Ryfast system, shortening travel between the city and surrounding islands by cutting through the fjord’s rocky bed."
